  "problem": "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-7x+n=4{x}^{2}-7x+2\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $n?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the constant terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the constant is $n.$ On the right-hand side, the constant is $2.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nn=2.\n$$",
